            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nEverything works as expected here. The `config.list` entry is for configuring [how visit index is converted to a path list by default](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d0464ced00abfd9bbed196fa36ccf3b1691c6b2c/doc/mini-visits.txt#L398). So although directory is indeed present in index, executing something like `:=MiniVisits.list_paths()` lists only files.\n\nThe reason for this design is mostly to reduce config duplication (as I'd imagine being able to configure which paths are listed would still be useful) and for performance. If the directory is not visited, it will be later automatically removed during pruning.\n\nIf you don't want directories to appear in the index directly, use [`remove_path`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d0464ced00abfd9bbed196fa36ccf3b1691c6b2c/doc/mini-visits.txt#L509) to remove directory items.\n\nClosing as everything works as expected here.",
